  "question": {
    "text": "A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is dropped from a height&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math> above the ground. Simultaneously another particle of the same mass is thrown vertically upwards from the ground with a speed of&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <msqrt> <mrow> <mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math>. If they collide head-on completely inelastically, then the time taken for the combined mass to reach the ground is"
  },
